                <pb facs="0939" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/713: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-22T15:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 25,
                            8.32 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Confirming my June 20, 6 p.m. Consul Lawton arrived here last night.</p>
                <p>It is reported that Federico Tinoco told the Latin American diplomats last night
                    that he had things well in hand here in [omission?] that he could quickly
                    suppress the invasion and the gunboat was going soon as also Consul Chase and he
                    had no reason for quitting as the greatest part of American interests were
                    supporting him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
